  73:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c **** 
  74:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c **** /**
  75:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * @brief  Initiates the stop procedure for Motor 1.
  76:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *
  77:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *  If the state machine is in #RUN or #START states the command is immediately
  78:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * executed. Otherwise, the command is discarded. The Application can check the
  79:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * return value to know whether the command was executed or discarded.
  80:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *
  81:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * @note The MCI_StopMotor1() command only triggers the stop motor procedure
  82:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * moving Motor 1's state machine to #ANY_STOP and then returns. It is not
  83:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * blocking the application until the motor is indeed stopped. To know if it has
  84:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * stopped, the application can query Motor 1's state machine ans check if the
  85:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * #IDLE state has been reached back.
  86:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *
  87:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * @retval returns true if the command is successfully executed, false otherwise.
  88:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   */
  89:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c **** __weak bool MC_StopMotor1(void)
  90:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c **** {
