 129:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c **** 
 130:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c **** /**
 131:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * @brief Programs a torque ramp for Motor 1 for later or immediate execution.
 132:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *
 133:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *  A torque ramp is a linear change from the current torque reference to the @p hFinalTorque
 134:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * target torque reference in the given @p hDurationms time.
 135:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *
 136:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *  Invoking the MC_ProgramTorqueRampMotor1() function programs a new torque ramp
 137:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * with the provided parameters. The programmed ramp is executed immediately if
 138:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * Motor 1's state machine is in the #START_RUN or #RUN states. Otherwise, the
 139:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * ramp is buffered and will be executed when the state machine reaches any of
 140:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * the aforementioned state.
 141:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *
 142:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *  The Application can check the status of the command with the MC_GetCommandStateMotor1()
 143:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * to know whether the last command was executed immediately or not.
 144:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *
 145:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * Only one command can be buffered at any given time. If another ramp - whether a
 146:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * torque or a speed one - or if another buffered command is programmed before the
 147:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * current one has completed, the latter replaces the former.
 148:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *
 149:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * @note A ramp cannot reverse the rotation direction if the Application is using
 150:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * sensorless motor control techniques. If the sign of the hFinalTorque parameter
 151:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * differs from that of the current torque, the ramp will not complete and a Speed
 152:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * Feedback error (#MC_SPEED_FDBK) will occur when the rotation speed is about to
 153:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * reach 0 rpm.
 154:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *
 155:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * @param  hFinalTorque Mechanical motor torque reference at the end of the ramp.
 156:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *         This value represents actually the Iq current expressed in digit.
 157:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   * @param  hDurationms Duration of the ramp expressed in milliseconds. It
 158:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *         is possible to set 0 to perform an instantaneous change in the torque
 159:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   *         value.
 160:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****   */
 161:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c **** __weak void MC_ProgramTorqueRampMotor1( int16_t hFinalTorque, uint16_t hDurationms )
 162:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c **** {
