 446:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c **** /**
 447:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * @brief Start the Encoder Alignment procedure for Motor 1, if possible
 448:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  *
 449:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  *  This command is used to trigger the encoder alignment procedure.
 450:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * If Motor 1's state machine is in #IDLE state, the command is immediately
 451:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * executed and true is returned. Otherwise, the command is discarded and false
 452:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * is returned.
 453:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  *
 454:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * @note The MC_AlignEncoderMotor1() command only triggers the alignment procedure:
 455:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * It moves Motor 1's state machine from the #IDLE to the #IDLE_ALIGNMENT state and
 456:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * then returns. It is not blocking the Application until the motor is indeed aligned.
 457:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * The Application can query Motor 1's state machine to check if the alignment
 458:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * procedure has completed: it is the case when the state machine is back to the #IDLE
 459:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * state.
 460:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  *
 461:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * See MC_GetSTMStateMotor1() for more details.
 462:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  *
 463:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  * @retval true if the command is successfully executed, false otherwise.
 464:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/src/MotorControl/mc_api.c ****  */
